KZ3 patch 2200 (RSX pass 173): the backend texture-component remap maps Y16_X16_FLOAT (0x9F) as {0,1,0,1}.
libs/video/rsx_texture_layout.c rsx_texture_component_remap: base 0x9F fell through lanes_argb {3,0,1,2}; RPCS3
VKFormats.cpp get_component_mapping maps Y16_X16_FLOAT as {R,G,R,G} (ARGB order: A=comp0, R=comp1, G=comp0, B=comp1)
over an R16G16 image whose component 0 is the first memory half (Y), so the sampler presents X in R and Y in G.
This is upstream ps3recomp PR #836 (sp00nznet/ps3recomp, MIT, by MatRanc), taken unchanged. It only affects the
D3D12 backend path (rsx_d3d12_backend.c) and the Vulkan/Metal ones; the live-draw engine has its own mapping
(ld_float_tex_mapping), fixed together with patch 2065's compute pass in patch 2201. Host test
tools/smoke/test_y16x16f.sh. Upstream candidate (already upstream as a PR).

diff --git a/libs/video/rsx_texture_layout.c b/libs/video/rsx_texture_layout.c
index 51a30a23..e79dcd8a 100644
--- a/libs/video/rsx_texture_layout.c
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_texture_layout.c
@@ -372,8 +372,13 @@ void rsx_texture_component_remap(u32 control1, u32 rsx_fmt, u8 out[4])
     static const u8 lanes_g8b8[4]  = {1, 0, 1, 0};
     static const u8 lanes_b8[4]    = {RSX_REMAP_ONE, 0, 0, 0};
     static const u8 lanes_depth[4] = {0, 0, 0, 0};
+    /* Y16_X16_FLOAT (0x9F): Y is the high half of the big-endian word, X the
+     * low half, and decode keeps memory order (resource 0 = Y, 1 = X), while
+     * the sampler presents X first (X, Y, X, Y). */
+    static const u8 lanes_y16x16f[4] = {0, 1, 0, 1};
     const u32 base = rsx_fmt & 0x9Fu;
-    const u8* src2res = (base == 0x8Bu) ? lanes_g8b8
+    const u8* src2res = (base == 0x9Fu) ? lanes_y16x16f
+                      : (base == 0x8Bu) ? lanes_g8b8
                       : (base == 0x81u || base == 0x94u) ? lanes_b8
                       : (base >= 0x90u && base <= 0x93u) ? lanes_depth : lanes_argb;
 
